# Indian Sign Language Recognition Using Deep Learning

## Project Overview
This project uses Deep Learning and Machine Learning techniques to recognize Indian Sign Language (ISL) hand signs from images. The project compares different models and identifies the best-performing model for sign classification.

## Project Objective
- Recognize Indian Sign Language hand signs from images.
- Explore and preprocess the image dataset.
- Build and compare Deep Learning models.
- Compare traditional Machine Learning algorithms.
- Evaluate model performance using classification metrics.

## Dataset
- **Total Images:** 4,972
- **Number of Classes:** 24
- **Validation Images:** 985

The dataset is organized into folders representing different sign classes.

## Models Used

### Deep Learning
- Custom Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)
- MobileNetV2
- EfficientNetB0

### Machine Learning
- Support Vector Machine (SVM)
- K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)
- Random Forest
- Logistic Regression

## Best Model Results

The final verified model is Fine-Tuned MobileNetV2.

| Metric | Score |
|---|---:|
| Accuracy | 97.56% |
| Precision | 97.72% |
| Recall | 97.56% |
| F1-Score | 97.53% |

